### 1. Unpack and set up
Extract the archive. Source OpenFOAM 5. cd into mesh/ - both fluid_regions_OF_m.stl and impeller.stl are already in constant/triSurface/.

### 2. Build the mesh with the impeller obstacle
rm -rf constant/polyMesh constant/extendedFeatureEdgeMesh, then: surfaceFeatureExtract, blockMesh, snappyHexMesh -overwrite, checkMesh -allTopology -allGeometry. This is a genuinely new mesh (impeller is a new internal obstacle) - watch for the impeller patch appearing with a sensible nonzero face count, and check the log for any indication the shaft/blades weren't cleanly carved out.

### 3. Build the rotor zone and split the outlet
rm -f constant/polyMesh/sets/*, then: topoSet (builds rotor cellSet + outletPort/outletDome faceSets), createPatch -overwrite (splits outlet into outlet_port + domeWall), rm -f constant/polyMesh/sets/outletPort constant/polyMesh/sets/outletPortCells constant/polyMesh/sets/outletDome, setsToZones, checkMesh.

### 4. Verify before proceeding
grep -A5 outlet_port and domeWall in constant/polyMesh/boundary (expect ~360/~990 split), confirm impeller patch face count looks reasonable, and confirm rotor cellZone size via the awk one-liner from before. Load in ParaView with Read Zones enabled and visually confirm the shaft+blades appear as a real hole through the mesh, not a solid lump (i.e. confirm the flood-fill castellation actually excluded it).

### 5. Assemble the run case
Copy case/0, case/constant, case/system into a run directory, then copy mesh/constant/polyMesh (with cellZones and split patches) into that directory's constant/polyMesh

### 6. Run
pimpleFoam | tee log.pimpleFoam. Watch Courant number, continuity errors, and confirm the MRF zone and impeller BC both load without error at startup.